hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1017","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, Yazid told us, and he is the son of Harun, Hammad bin Salamah told us, and Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Abu Al-Walid, Hammad bin Salamah said, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya, also Abu al-Nu’man told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Abu Naamah, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying, so he took off his shoes, so the people took them off. Their shoes. When he left, he said: “Why did you take off your shoes?” They said: O Messenger of God, we saw you took them off, so we took off. He said: “Gabriel came to me. So he told me that there is impurity in them, so when one of you comes to the mosque, he should turn his shoes around, and if he sees any impurity in them, he should wipe them with the ground. Then let him pray in it.” This is the hadith of Yazid bin Harun, and Muhammad bin Yahya said in the hadith of Abu Al-Walid, and he said: “Gabriel told me that “There is filth or harm in them.”"
